Supermarket Sales Analysis
1. Introduction

This project is based on the analysis of supermarket sales data. The dataset contains 500 sales transactions with details such as product, category, branch, city, customer type, payment method, quantity, sales and rating.

The main purpose of the project is to understand sales performance and find useful patterns from the data.

2. Objectives
Analyze overall supermarket sales.
Find the best-performing products and categories.
Compare sales between different branches and cities.
Analyze customer types and payment methods.
Calculate important sales KPIs.
Create charts and an interactive Power BI dashboard.
3. Tools Used
Microsoft Excel – Data cleaning and preparation
Python – Data analysis
Pandas – Data processing
Matplotlib – Charts and visualization
Power BI – Dashboard and interactive analysis
DAX – KPI calculations
4. Dataset

The dataset contains 500 transactions and 13 columns, including:

Invoice ID, Date, Branch, City, Customer Type, Gender, Product, Category, Quantity, Unit Price, Payment, Rating and Sales.

The data was checked for missing values, duplicates and sales calculation errors before analysis.

5. Key Results
Metric	Result
Total Sales	₹244,411.08
Transactions	500
Quantity Sold	2,768
Average Transaction	₹488.82
Average Rating	3.99/5

Some important findings were:

Cheese had the highest product sales – ₹27,906.30.
Branch C (Mumbai) had the highest sales – ₹72,469.45.
Beverages was the highest-selling category – ₹56,108.24.
UPI was the most-used payment method with 127 transactions.
6. Power BI Dashboard

The Power BI dashboard contains KPI cards and charts for:

Total Sales
Total Transactions
Quantity Sold
Average Transaction
Average Rating
Sales by Product
Sales by Branch
Sales by Category
Payment Methods
Customer Type
City-wise Sales

Filters were also added for Branch, City, Category, Payment, Customer Type and Gender.

7. Conclusion

This project helped me understand how sales data can be cleaned, analyzed and converted into useful business insights. Python was used for analysis and Power BI was used to create an interactive dashboard.

The project also helped me gain practical experience in Excel, Python, Pandas, Data Visualization, DAX and Power BI.